WEBVTT

00:12.810 --> 00:15.570
Is this the palace of Idanokan?

00:15.570 --> 00:18.110
Were we able to make it back?

00:18.110 --> 00:20.660
It's so dark, I can hardly see.

00:24.020 --> 00:24.950
Amber?

00:30.490 --> 00:32.360
There are no monsters nearby.

00:32.830 --> 00:34.760
There's nothing living, either.

00:35.390 --> 00:37.140
Are you feeling sad?

00:39.710 --> 00:41.080
Be careful.

00:41.080 --> 00:42.180
I smell blood.

00:44.140 --> 00:45.180
Huh?

00:47.530 --> 00:49.010
I'm blinded!

00:52.090 --> 00:53.850
Is this better?

00:53.850 --> 00:54.540
Yeah.

01:09.310 --> 01:12.100
This armor... belongs to imperial soldiers.

01:12.550 --> 01:14.850
They must have fought the monsters here.

01:15.470 --> 01:18.360
They couldn't even bury their dead?

01:18.850 --> 01:20.940
Just how intense was the fighting?

01:21.680 --> 01:25.430
It's possible this world is already...

01:29.370 --> 01:30.260
What's wrong?

01:39.410 --> 01:41.120
Go!

01:41.420 --> 01:42.820
The Imperial Army!

01:42.820 --> 01:45.120
There are some still engaged in combat?!

01:45.120 --> 01:46.790
Satou, over there!

01:48.010 --> 01:49.140
Satou?

01:51.010 --> 01:51.750
Yeah.

01:52.090 --> 01:53.100
I know.

01:56.590 --> 01:58.190
The Abyss King.

03:45.910 --> 03:49.590
If you go down through here, you'll come out 
on the flank of the monster horde.

03:50.060 --> 03:52.280
You'll be able to catch 
the Abyss King by surprise.

03:52.280 --> 03:52.940
Yeah.

03:53.720 --> 03:54.990
Satou.

03:54.990 --> 03:56.090
Don't worry.

03:56.530 --> 03:58.060
We have all the rings.

03:58.590 --> 04:00.090
I have everyone's power.

04:00.810 --> 04:02.920
This is sooner than we expected,

04:03.410 --> 04:05.020
but this is what we returned home for.

04:09.670 --> 04:11.550
Please, Ring King.

04:11.970 --> 04:14.600
I'm betting everything on you.

04:14.990 --> 04:18.070
I'm sure you'll be fine, Satou-sama.

04:18.070 --> 04:18.860
Yeah.

04:21.790 --> 04:24.100
We're counting on you, Ring King.

04:31.720 --> 04:32.690
Satou.

04:42.920 --> 04:45.490
I'll be waiting, okay?

04:47.720 --> 04:48.970
All right.

04:49.790 --> 04:50.770
I'll be going.

05:16.540 --> 05:17.910
You're here,

05:19.630 --> 05:21.560
Inheritor of the Rings?

05:35.630 --> 05:37.730
You've done well to make it this far.

05:38.610 --> 05:41.470
Boy, new King,

05:41.980 --> 05:44.250
I'll unite your power.

05:53.620 --> 05:54.890
Wow...

06:05.420 --> 06:08.060
This time, hold nothing back.

06:55.510 --> 06:56.610
He did it!

06:58.060 --> 06:58.950
No.

07:04.490 --> 07:06.670
No way...

07:07.280 --> 07:08.710
How?!

07:09.350 --> 07:12.740
The Rings are the manifestation 
of the world's order.

07:13.250 --> 07:15.880
The Abyss is supposed to perish,

07:15.880 --> 07:19.500
and the world is supposed to be saved...

07:21.460 --> 07:25.630
Does this mean... I'm not good enough?!

07:26.630 --> 07:27.800
Satou!

07:30.620 --> 07:32.720
Inheritor of the Rings.

07:33.400 --> 07:37.090
So, you are another ignorant puppet?

07:37.960 --> 07:38.850
Oh, no!

07:39.350 --> 07:41.270
No, this can't be!

07:41.880 --> 07:43.660
What about our duty?!

07:44.230 --> 07:46.660
What happened to the legends?!

07:47.580 --> 07:48.990
I'm going!

07:48.990 --> 07:51.570
We can't afford to lose Satou here!

07:58.850 --> 07:59.870
Don't worry.

08:00.280 --> 08:01.950
I won't let him die.

08:07.150 --> 08:12.090
So, it really is possible to be unable 
to move a single finger...

08:16.480 --> 08:18.350
Return to the Abyss.

08:43.550 --> 08:46.790
Women of the Rings...

08:47.970 --> 08:51.000
Everyone? Why are you here?

08:51.000 --> 08:52.840
You think we'd just abandon you?!

09:26.500 --> 09:27.710
Granart!

09:29.670 --> 09:31.630
Damn it! Let me go!

09:45.290 --> 09:47.850
Tsk! There are too many.

10:02.090 --> 10:02.910
Satou!

10:02.910 --> 10:04.040
Satou-sama!

10:04.710 --> 10:05.610
Everyone...

10:06.440 --> 10:07.610
I'm sorry.

10:07.610 --> 10:08.790
Satou!

10:12.780 --> 10:14.040
Hime!

10:35.710 --> 10:37.250
Good morning, Satou.

10:40.600 --> 10:41.810
Hime...

10:42.670 --> 10:43.890
Good morning.

10:51.270 --> 11:00.590
Do you promise to love and to cherish 
one another, in sickness and in health?

11:00.990 --> 11:02.130
I do.

12:02.100 --> 12:03.210
Grandpa?

12:04.020 --> 12:06.990
You're awake, Satou-kun?

12:07.790 --> 12:11.060
Oh... I guess I died?

12:11.840 --> 12:14.030
What are you saying?

12:14.030 --> 12:16.270
We haven't died yet.

12:18.380 --> 12:20.020
What's this?

12:20.670 --> 12:22.930
Alabaster-dono saved us.

12:23.330 --> 12:25.300
That's the Great Sage for you.

12:25.550 --> 12:27.160
What are you saying?

12:27.160 --> 12:28.260
I'm not that great.

12:28.890 --> 12:32.100
Creating an opening and getting 
you all away from the Abyss King

12:32.100 --> 12:35.050
was the best I could manage.

12:36.510 --> 12:40.270
We really do need the
 Ring King's power, after all.

12:41.690 --> 12:45.160
Oh, yeah! If you're safe, 
then that means Marse-san is...!

12:45.480 --> 12:47.820
Prince Marse is safe, too, yes.

12:50.200 --> 12:53.350
It's all thanks to this one.

12:55.580 --> 12:56.750
You're...

12:57.480 --> 13:00.270
It's been a while, Ring King.

13:00.680 --> 13:02.680
I'm from Wind's royal family of Romca,

13:02.680 --> 13:04.920
Smaragdi Romca.

13:05.700 --> 13:08.110
Thanks to Smaragdi,

13:08.110 --> 13:14.230
we managed to escape from 
the Abyss Monsters that surrounded us.

13:15.330 --> 13:19.650
I've been watching over 
Alabaster-sama for a while.

13:20.060 --> 13:22.810
However, once he was faced with danger...

13:22.810 --> 13:24.790
I couldn't sit still.

13:25.570 --> 13:30.890
Because of that, 
I was able to aid Alabaster-sama.

13:30.890 --> 13:36.400
Alabaster-sama gave my life 
such wonderful meaning.

13:36.400 --> 13:38.790
To me, he truly is my one...

13:43.170 --> 13:46.500
The monsters have withdrawn.

13:46.500 --> 13:50.100
I believe the Abyss King 
has suffered a serious wound, too.

13:50.520 --> 13:53.600
I guess I at least had some effect.

13:53.600 --> 13:55.310
What are you saying?

13:55.310 --> 13:57.790
It was wonderfully effective.

13:57.790 --> 14:02.440
We couldn't even get 
a single arrow to pierce him.

14:03.240 --> 14:06.040
You've done well, Satou-kun.

14:07.980 --> 14:12.660
Great Sage, what is the overall situation like?

14:13.010 --> 14:14.960
Shortly after you left,

14:14.960 --> 14:19.150
the Abyss King's forces 
commenced their invasion,

14:19.150 --> 14:23.660
and the Imperial Army halted their advance 
at the Great Mountain Wall.

14:23.660 --> 14:25.560
I assisted, but...

14:25.940 --> 14:29.380
there was little we could do 
other than run away.

14:29.380 --> 14:30.660
And Maasa?!

14:30.660 --> 14:32.350
What happened to Maasa?!

14:32.730 --> 14:37.420
Each nation is fighting in different locations.

14:37.420 --> 14:39.500
Maasa is safe.

14:39.500 --> 14:42.310
Prince Marse is there, as well.

14:42.770 --> 14:48.410
Though the number of monsters 
just keeps going up, not down.

14:48.410 --> 14:50.910
The situation is steadily worsening.

14:51.330 --> 14:55.120
I'm really glad we didn't give up hope.

14:55.990 --> 14:58.600
I'm glad you all made it back!

14:59.400 --> 15:02.330
Alabaster-sama, it's almost dawn.

15:02.760 --> 15:05.050
The Ring King has returned.

15:05.360 --> 15:07.760
All the princesses are together, too.

15:08.040 --> 15:11.790
The morning sun is full of hope.

15:18.920 --> 15:21.200
The Ring King has returned!

15:21.200 --> 15:23.380
All five princesses are with him!

15:26.190 --> 15:29.980
I was told I couldn't go outside 
because there's lots of monsters.

15:29.980 --> 15:34.280
But it'll be okay now that 
you're back, right, Ring King?

15:34.790 --> 15:36.910
Yeah, leave it to me.

15:38.090 --> 15:40.250
I'll save this world!

15:44.100 --> 15:48.650
Now, we need to talk about what's to come.

15:48.650 --> 15:52.380
Before that, I'd like to hear your excuse.

15:52.780 --> 15:55.090
I thought we were supposed 
to be able to defeat the Abyss King

15:55.090 --> 15:57.220
once the Rings were collected?

15:57.220 --> 16:00.230
<b>STARE...</b>

16:00.230 --> 16:02.890
Grandpa, be honest with me.

16:03.330 --> 16:05.440
Was my power not enough?

16:05.800 --> 16:11.570
I have one idea as to why you 
weren't able to defeat the Abyss King.

16:12.020 --> 16:19.400
There was not one mention of 
the Black Rings that the Abyss King wore.

16:19.920 --> 16:21.370
Black Rings?

16:21.900 --> 16:24.920
They looked just like this, only black.

16:25.180 --> 16:27.130
That's not in my records.

16:27.570 --> 16:30.010
The dwarves didn't know about that, either.

16:30.660 --> 16:34.010
Still, even in multiple sources,

16:34.010 --> 16:38.350
it's certain that the Ring King 
sealed away the Abyss King.

16:38.350 --> 16:43.850
However, we don't know how much 
power was required to do so.

16:43.850 --> 16:46.290
Then what are you saying we should do?

16:46.290 --> 16:48.650
There's only one thing we can do.

16:49.160 --> 16:53.740
We have to draw out even more of 
the Rings' power before our next battle!

16:53.740 --> 16:59.120
Which means Satou-kun needs to strengthen his
bonds with the Ring Princesses even further.

16:59.370 --> 17:02.370
Even stronger bonds... Does that mean...?

17:02.680 --> 17:03.980
Baby making!

17:04.580 --> 17:06.530
Well, that's one option.

17:06.530 --> 17:07.790
It is?!

17:08.080 --> 17:09.630
Satou-kun!

17:09.630 --> 17:11.020
Marse-san!

17:11.020 --> 17:12.170
What are you doing here?!

17:12.920 --> 17:16.840
I received word that you 
had returned, and came at once.

17:17.160 --> 17:19.980
I wanted to see you as soon as possible.

17:21.450 --> 17:24.770
Now, moving on to the main topic.

17:26.890 --> 17:32.540
It's said that the Ring Princesses stood 
alongside the Ring King in battle long ago.

17:33.100 --> 17:35.930
In order to draw out the Rings' power,

17:36.150 --> 17:38.280
both the will to fight alongside him

17:38.280 --> 17:43.540
and the strength to carry out 
that will may be required.

17:43.850 --> 17:45.110
Strength, huh?

17:45.640 --> 17:48.500
Saphir, Amber, and I may be fine there...

17:48.500 --> 17:50.800
But we're not very helpful.

17:50.800 --> 17:52.090
So, on that note,

17:52.430 --> 17:57.550
we'll have everyone acquire the strength 
that befits a wife of the Ring King!

17:57.890 --> 18:01.760
That's right, this training...

18:02.290 --> 18:05.150
is wife training!

18:11.810 --> 18:14.860
This will be your room, Ring King.

18:15.100 --> 18:17.580
The Princesses are already waiting for you.

18:29.770 --> 18:34.880
Satou, once again, you made up your mind 
to fight to save this world for our sakes.

18:34.880 --> 18:38.840
So I believe we should 
steel our resolve, as well.

18:39.130 --> 18:42.930
Ring King, replenish your energy 
as much as you need.

18:43.210 --> 18:45.770
Now, choose the woman you'd like!

18:45.770 --> 18:48.640
Of course, you're welcome 
to choose all of us at once!

18:48.640 --> 18:50.060
Huh?

18:50.420 --> 18:53.920
What's the matter? 
Isn't a harem every man's dream?!

18:53.920 --> 18:57.820
Look at what you're doing. 
You're troubling the Ring King.

18:59.340 --> 19:02.530
This is the problem with beastmen 
who can't read the mood.

19:02.530 --> 19:03.780
What?!

19:02.530 --> 19:03.780
<b>SNAP</b>

19:03.780 --> 19:05.020
What did you say?!

19:05.020 --> 19:07.770
That's big talk from the shorty 
who fell behind her little sister!

19:07.770 --> 19:10.650
Huh?! Saphira has nothing to do with this!

19:09.750 --> 19:13.180
What? Did I hit the mark? 
You're raising your voice so much.

19:13.180 --> 19:14.620
I am not!

19:20.040 --> 19:22.050
Bridal training, huh?

19:22.050 --> 19:24.100
You sound happy.

19:24.100 --> 19:25.730
Huh? Not particularly.

19:26.440 --> 19:29.180
You've been working 
so hard for us this whole time,

19:29.180 --> 19:31.140
so it's my turn to work hard, too.

19:37.070 --> 19:39.780
Is that...?

19:39.780 --> 19:40.500
Yeah.

19:43.480 --> 19:48.950
In my real family, I had a father, 
a mother, and a little sister.

19:49.830 --> 19:52.370
My little sister remained in this world,

19:52.850 --> 19:54.820
so I haven't seen her in ten years now.

19:56.340 --> 19:58.490
My parents are here.

19:59.990 --> 20:04.420
Father, Mother, I'm home.

20:05.160 --> 20:07.020
It happened when I was little.

20:07.020 --> 20:10.140
So I only vaguely remember 
what they looked like,

20:10.760 --> 20:15.220
but they both risked their lives to protect me.

20:20.550 --> 20:21.990
This man...

20:22.860 --> 20:24.550
is my husband.

20:26.220 --> 20:27.830
Thank you, Satou.

20:28.770 --> 20:32.600
I was able to return here, thanks to you.

20:36.500 --> 20:37.670
Krystal.

20:38.860 --> 20:41.210
Grandpa?! How long have you been there?!

20:41.700 --> 20:45.520
Since, "Father, Mother, I'm home."

20:45.520 --> 20:47.010
That's basically the whole time!

20:47.010 --> 20:50.380
I don't think it's anything 
to be embarrassed about.

20:50.380 --> 20:52.530
I think it was a lovely story.

20:53.130 --> 20:56.850
By the way, about your magic training.

20:56.850 --> 20:58.330
Yeah, I'll do my best!

20:58.330 --> 20:59.360
I'm counting on you!

20:59.360 --> 21:02.300
No, it won't be me.

21:02.820 --> 21:06.200
I've summoned a teacher 
more appropriate for you, Krystal.

21:06.860 --> 21:10.530
I wanted to let you know,
 since they should be arriving soon.

21:13.900 --> 21:14.870
What?!

21:28.450 --> 21:31.140
Hmm, so you're...

21:31.570 --> 21:33.320
You're not too bad.

21:38.770 --> 21:42.130
I'm Morion Ravri Nokanatika.

21:43.810 --> 21:45.030
Glad to see you,

21:45.340 --> 21:46.440
Sister.

21:47.690 --> 21:48.870
And...

21:49.300 --> 21:50.470
Brother.

21:52.540 --> 21:53.910
Brother?

21:54.620 --> 21:59.650
Morion Ravri Nokanatika?

22:01.010 --> 22:04.690
You're Hime's little sister?!
